<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Saint Ulrich of Augsburg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">890–973</span> · Also known as Ulrich of Augsburg, Udalric of Augsburg</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Saint Ulrich of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/augsburg">Augsburg</a> was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> of Augsburg from 923 to 973. He organised the defence of the city against the Hungarians in 955, holding out until King Otto I defeated them at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-lechfeld">Battle of Lechfeld</a>. In 993 he became the first person to be formally canonised by a pope, John XV, and he remains Augsburg's patron saint.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ulrich-of-augsburg.jpg" alt="Saint Ulrich of Augsburg" width="320" height="773" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Leonhard Beck · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Leonhard_Beck_-_Heiliger_Ulrich_(Veste_Coburg).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
